; 31-parse.kurt

; `parse` is `tokenize`'s (30-tokenize.kurt) sibling one stage further: it
; shows the actual tree-structured term an expression parses into (as an
; s-expression), plus the syntax declarations of every symbol involved.  It's
; the fastest way to check that an operator you just declared binds the way
; you think it does -- we'll lean on it heavily in the rest of this section.

bool A, B
parse A implies B
